BND-12: count TIMEOPEN / TIMECLOSED from the start of the run, not from midnight

SWMMEngine seeded every link's time_last_set with floor(start_date), the
start date at midnight, copying legacy link_initState(), so TIMEOPEN /
TIMECLOSED rule premises included the start time of day: in a run starting
at 06:00 every link had been open or closed for 6 h at the first step. Use
the start date-time, as the 5.3.0 patch does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-12_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..4f2a10c 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
